{"id":10078,"name":"groudon-primal","speciesId":383,"dex":383,"form":"other","generation":3,"types":["ground","fire"],"stats":{"hp":100,"attack":180,"defense":160,"special-attack":150,"special-defense":90,"speed":90},"abilities":[{"name":"desolate-land","hidden":false}],"height":50,"weight":9997,"baseExp":347,"sprites":{"normal":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/sprites/master/sprites/pokemon/other/official-artwork/10078.png","shiny":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/sprites/master/sprites/pokemon/other/official-artwork/shiny/10078.png","icon":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/sprites/master/sprites/pokemon/10078.png"},"cry":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/cries/main/cries/pokemon/latest/10078.ogg","genus":"Continent Pokémon","genusPt":"Pokémon do continente","flavor":[{"version":"ruby","text":"GROUDON has long been described in mythology as the POKéMON that raised lands and expanded continents. This POKéMON took to sleep after a cataclysmic battle with KYOGRE."},{"version":"sapphire","text":"GROUDON has the power to scatter rain clouds and make water evaporate with light and heat. It came as a savior to people who had been suffering from terrible floods."},{"version":"emerald","text":"GROUDON has appeared in mythology as the creator of the land. It sleeps in magma underground and is said to make volcanoes erupt on awakening."},{"version":"firered","text":"This legendary POKéMON is said to represent the land. It went to sleep after dueling KYOGRE."},{"version":"diamond","text":"It had been asleep in underground magma ever since it fiercely fought KYOGRE long ago."},{"version":"heartgold","text":"Said to have expanded the lands by evaporating water with raging heat. It battled titanically with KYOGRE."},{"version":"black","text":"It had been asleep in underground magma ever since it fiercely fought Kyogre long ago."},{"version":"x","text":"Said to have expanded the lands by evaporating water with raging heat. It battled titanically with Kyogre."},{"version":"y","text":"This legendary Pokémon is said to represent the land. It went to sleep after dueling Kyogre."},{"version":"omega-ruby","text":"Groudon is said to be the personification of the land itself. Legends tell of its many clashes against Kyogre, as each sought to gain the power of nature."},{"version":"alpha-sapphire","text":"Through Primal Reversion and with nature’s full power, it will take back its true form. It can cause magma to erupt and expand the landmass of the world."}],"flavorPt":"Através da Reversão Primal e com todo o poder da natureza, ele recuperará sua verdadeira forma. Pode causar a erupção do magma e expandir a massa terrestre do mundo.","genderRate":-1,"captureRate":3,"eggGroups":["no-eggs"],"isLegendary":true,"isMythical":false,"evolution":{"species":"groudon","speciesId":383,"evolvesTo":[]},"varieties":[{"id":383,"name":"groudon","form":"normal","sprite":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/sprites/master/sprites/pokemon/other/official-artwork/383.png"},{"id":10078,"name":"groudon-primal","form":"other","sprite":"https://raw.githubusercontent.com/PokeAPI/sprites/master/sprites/pokemon/other/official-artwork/10078.png"}],"games":[16,17,18],"moves":[{"id":7,"learn":[[16,"tutor",0],[18,"tutor",0]]},{"id":9,"learn":[[16,"tutor",0],[18,"tutor",0]]},{"id":14,"learn":[[16,"tm",0],[17,"tm",0],[18,"tm",0]]},{"id":15,"learn":[[16,"tm",0]]},{"id":46,"learn":[[16,"tm",0],[17,"tm",0],[18,"tm",0]]},{"id":53,"learn":[[16,"tm",0],[17,"tm",0],[18,"tm",0]]},{"id":63,"learn":[[16,"tm",0],[17,"tm",0],[18,"tm",0]]},{"id":70,"learn":[[16,"tm",0]]},{"id":76,"learn":[[16,"lv",60],[16,"tm",0],[17,"lv",60],[17,"tm",0],[18,"lv",60],[18,"tm",0]]},{"id":85,"learn":[[16,"tm",0],[17,"tm",0],[18,"tm",0]]},{"id":86,"learn":[[16,"tm",0],[17,"tm",0],[18,"tm",0]]},{"id":87,"learn":[[16,"tm",0],[17,"tm",0],[18,"tm",0]]},{"id":89,"learn":[[16,"lv",35],[16,"tm",0],[17,"lv",35],[17,"tm",0],[18,"lv",35],[18,"tm",0]]},{"id":90,"learn":[[16,"lv",65]